For the implementation I am thinking of simply calling `FileStreamHelpers.FlushToDisk(handle)` which automatically does the right thing [for Windows](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/5a24757eab72279dcc28f2359ef5771b279efc59/src/libraries/System.Private.CoreLib/src/System/IO/Strategies/FileStreamHelpers.Windows.cs#L39) and [for Unix](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/5a24757eab72279dcc28f2359ef5771b279efc59/src/libraries/System.Private.CoreLib/src/System/IO/Strategies/FileStreamHelpers.Unix.cs#L40). This is the same helper function used by `FileStream.Flush(bool)` and I think it makes sense to share the logic...**please let me know if there's a better or more preferred way** 👍

My prototype looks like this:

```csharp
public static void FlushToDisk(SafeFileHandle handle)
{
   ValidateInput(handle, fileOffset: 0);

   FileStreamHelpers.FlushToDisk(handle);
}
```

